    <body>

        <section name="Download latest DavMail Gateway release">
            <p>The right DavMail package choice depends on your operating system and
                deployment (server or workstation).
            </p>
            <p>Please consider making a donation to help this project at
                <a href="https://www.paypal.com/donate/?business=UWPTTD99YF6D6&amp;no_recurring=0&amp;item_name=DavMail+POP%2FIMAP%2FSMTP%2FCalDAV%2FCardDAV%2FLDAP+Exchange+and+Office+365+Gateway&amp;currency_code=USD"
                   title="Donate">
                    <img alt="Donate dollars" src="https://img.shields.io/badge/paypal-donate-green.svg"/>
                </a>

                <a href="https://www.paypal.com/donate/?business=UWPTTD99YF6D6&amp;no_recurring=0&amp;item_name=DavMail+POP%2FIMAP%2FSMTP%2FCalDAV%2FCardDAV%2FLDAP+Exchange+and+Office+365+Gateway&amp;currency_code=EUR"
                   title="Donate">
                    <img alt="Donate euros" src="https://img.shields.io/badge/paypal-donate-green.svg"/>
                </a>
            </p>

            <subsection name="Workstation (personal) mode">
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Windows:</strong>
                        Download installation package:
                        <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">davmail-<em>version</em>-setup64.exe
                        </a> or noinstall zip:
                        <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">davmail-<em>version</em>-windows-standalone.zip
                        </a>
                        which now both include Azul JDK, and follow instructions at
                        <a href="windowssetup.html">DavMail Setup on Windows</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>macOS:</strong>
                        Setup Azul JDK FX from <a href="https://www.azul.com/downloads/?os=macos&amp;package=jdk-fx">Azul Downloads</a>,
                        then download
                        <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">DavMail-MacOSX-<em>version</em>.app.zip</a>
                        <br/>
                        and follow instructions at
                        <a href="macosxsetup.html">DavMail Setup on macOS</a><br/>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Linux Flatpak:</strong>
                        DavMail can be installed as a Flatpak:

                        <a href="https://flathub.org/en/apps/org.davmail.DavMail">DavMail Flatpak package</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Linux OpenSUSE:</strong>
                        RPM packages are available from OpenSUSE build service:

                        <a href="https://software.opensuse.org/download.html?project=home%3Amguessan%3Adavmail&amp;package=davmail">OpenSUSE DavMail Package</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Linux Fedora and RedHat:</strong>
                        DavMail Fedora packages are available on COPR:

                        <a href="https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/mguessan/davmail">Fedora DavMail package</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Debian Linux (and Debian-based distributions like Ubuntu):</strong>
                        Download debian package
                        <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">davmail_<em>version</em>-1_all.deb
                        </a>
                        <br/>
                        and follow instructions at
                        <a href="linuxsetup.html">DavMail Setup on Linux</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Docker:</strong>
                        Docker images are available on GitHub Container Registry:
                        <a href="https://github.com/mguessan/davmail/pkgs/container/davmail">DavMail Docker image</a>

                        More details at:
                        <a href="https://github.com/mguessan/davmail/tree/master/src/docker/README.md">DavMail Docker instructions</a>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Other:</strong>
                        Download platform independent package
                        <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">davmail-<em>version</em>.zip
                        </a>
                        <br/>
                        and follow instructions at
                        <a href="linuxsetup.html">DavMail Setup on linux</a>
                        <br/>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </subsection>

            <subsection name="Server (shared) mode">
                <p>
                        Download standalone package for Windows:
                        <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">davmail-<em>version</em>-windows-standalone.zip
                        </a>
                        or platform independent package for other operating systems:
                        <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">davmail-<em>version</em>.zip
                        </a>.
                        Docker packages are also available, see above.
                        <br/>
                        Follow server mode setup instructions at
                        <a href="serversetup.html">DavMail Setup as a standalone server</a>
                        <br/>
                </p>
            </subsection>

            <subsection name="Build from source">
                <p>
                    Download source tarball
                    <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/davmail/files/">davmail-src-<em>version</em>.tgz
                    </a>
                    <br/>
                    and follow instructions at
                    <a href="build.html">Building DavMail from source</a>
                    <br/>
                </p>
            </subsection>
        </section>

    </body>
